# Design System & Visual Identity

## Design Philosophy

Vyayamy is a **calm, minimal workout journal**. Every design decision follows this priority order — never invert it:

1. **Clarity** — the user should instantly understand what they're looking at
2. **Usability** — every interaction should feel obvious and forgiving
3. **Speed** — perceived and actual; no layout jank, no unnecessary spinners
4. **Consistency** — identical patterns for identical actions, everywhere
5. **Delight** — subtle motion and refined details, earned only after the above are satisfied

### Foundational Principles

**Dieter Rams — remove everything unnecessary.** Fewer buttons, fewer visual elements, more whitespace. If an element doesn't serve the user's current task, it shouldn't be on screen.

**Don Norman — match human mental models.** Behavior must be predictable. Labels must be clear. Actions must be obvious.

**Apple Health aesthetic.** Restrained, typographic, spacious — not typical fitness-app design. Inspirations: Apple Health, Apple Fitness, Whoop, Strava, Strong, Hevy.

### Non-negotiables

- **Single column**, phone-first; no tablet-specific layouts
- **Warm neutral palette** — stone/amber tones (`#F8F8F6` bg, `#1C1917` text)
- **System font** (React Native default — San Francisco on iOS, Roboto on Android). No custom fonts.
- **44pt minimum touch target** (`theme.touch.min`) on every interactive element
- **Generous whitespace** — when in doubt, add more
- **Subtle motion** only — 150 / 250 / 350 ms durations (`theme.duration`). No bouncy springs, no particles.
- **Progressive disclosure** — primary action visible; secondary actions revealed on interaction

## Styling Rules

All tokens live in `src/ui/theme.ts` as a plain TypeScript object. There are **no CSS files in the mobile app**. Styling happens via `StyleSheet.create` at the bottom of the component file.

### Always use tokens

```ts
// Correct
import { theme } from '@/ui/theme';

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  card: {
    padding: theme.space.s4,
    backgroundColor: theme.color.surface,
    borderRadius: theme.radius.md,
  },
  title: {
    fontSize: theme.font.section,
    fontWeight: theme.font.weight.semibold,
    color: theme.color.text,
  },
});
```

```ts
// Wrong — hard-coded values
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  card: { padding: 16, backgroundColor: '#FFFFFF', borderRadius: 12 },
});
```

### Token surface (from `src/ui/theme.ts`)

| Category | Tokens                                                                                                  |
| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Color    | `bg`, `surface`, `text`, `textSecondary`, `textTertiary`, `border`, `borderStrong`, `accent`, `accentMuted`, `success`, `danger`, `pr`, `onAccent`, `overlay` |
| Space    | `s1` (4) → `s12` (48), `page` (20), `section` (32), `half` (2)                                          |
| Radius   | `sm` (8), `md` (12), `lg` (16), `full` (9999)                                                           |
| Font     | `display`, `title`, `section`, `card`, `body`, `meta`, `micro`; `weight.medium/semibold/bold`           |
| Touch    | `min` (44), `navHeight` (64)                                                                            |
| Duration | `fast` (150), `normal` (250), `slow` (350)                                                              |

## Components and Interactions

### Pressables

Use `Pressable` for everything interactive. Express pressed state via a function style prop:

```tsx
<Pressable
  onPress={onStart}
  style={({ pressed }) => [styles.cta, pressed && styles.ctaPressed]}
>
  <Text style={styles.ctaText}>Start workout</Text>
</Pressable>
```

Keep the pressed effect subtle — a lighter background or `opacity: 0.9`. No scale-on-press bounces.

### Feedback

- Haptics via `expo-haptics` for meaningful events: set completed (`ImpactFeedbackStyle.Medium`), PR achieved (`NotificationFeedbackType.Success`), destructive confirmation (`ImpactFeedbackStyle.Heavy`)
- Background rest cue via the local notification in `src/lib/restNotifications.ts`
- Toasts via `ToastProvider` (`useToast()`) — do NOT use `Alert.alert` for transient feedback

### Charts

Charts are in-house SVG. Use `src/ui/LineChart.tsx` or extend it — do not add Recharts or `victory-native`. Axes, ticks, and labels use `theme.color.chartAxis` / `textTertiary`.

### Icons

SVG icons via `react-native-svg`, centralized in `src/ui/TabIcon.tsx` and similar components. No icon libraries with per-glyph imports (no `@expo/vector-icons` sprawl).

## Layout Defaults

- Screens: `SafeAreaView` → `ScrollView` with `contentContainerStyle: { padding: theme.space.page, gap: theme.space.s4 }`
- Cards: `backgroundColor: theme.color.surface`, `borderRadius: theme.radius.md`, `borderWidth: 1`, `borderColor: theme.color.border`, `padding: theme.space.s4`
- Primary CTA: `backgroundColor: theme.color.accent`, `color: theme.color.onAccent`, `height: 52`, `borderRadius: theme.radius.md`

## Responsive

Phone-first. No media queries, no `Dimensions`-based layout branching unless strictly needed. Keep everything single-column and let `flex` handle the rest.

## Grandfathered Exceptions

Short prefixes on legacy components (`hd-`, `pg-`, `esm-`) existed only in the old CSS world and do not apply to the RN codebase. Use descriptive component and style names everywhere.
